# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. On Windows, a CRLF checkout of a script
# with a `#!/usr/bin/env bash` shebang fails to run at all — bash reads the \r as
# part of the interpreter name and reports "bad interpreter" / "no such file".
*.sh text eol=lf
*.command text eol=lf

# Normalize Markdown to LF in the repository. AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md must stay
# byte-identical (scripts/check-agent-instructions.sh enforces it); without this,
# an editor that rewrites one file's endings makes the two blobs differ for a
# reason that has nothing to do with their content.
*.md text=auto eol=lf
